          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "question": {
            "text": "If ${}^{n}C_4, {}^{n}C_5$ and ${}^{n}C_6$ are in arithmetic progression (A.P.), then the value of n is...",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "OQmaX",
              "label": "A",
              "text": "$5$ or $11$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "WG8z9",
              "label": "B",
              "text": "$7$ or $14$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "na4Db",
              "label": "C",
              "text": "$8$ or $15$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "7aAou",
              "label": "D",
              "text": "$6$ or $13$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Given that $^{n}C_4, ^{n}C_5, ^{n}C_6$ are in A.P.<br><br>$2 \\times ^{n}C_5 = ^{n}C_4 + ^{n}C_6$<br><br>$2 \\times \\dfrac{n!}{5!(n-5)!} = \\dfrac{n!}{4!(n-4)!} + \\dfrac{n!}{6!(n-6)!}$<br><br>Multiplying the entire equation by $\\dfrac{6!(n-4)!}{n!}$:<br><br>$2 \\times 6 \\times (n-4) = 6 \\times 5 + (n-4)(n-5)$<br><br>$12n - 48 = 30 + n^2 - 9n + 20$<br><br>$n^2 - 21n + 98 = 0$<br><br>$(n-7)(n-14) = 0$<br><br>$n = 7$ or $n = 14$<br><br>Answer: $7$ or $14$",
            "image": null
          },
