          "question": {
            "text": "The value of ${ }^{47} C_4+\\sum_{j=1}^5{ }^{(52-j)} C_3$ is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "aCF94",
              "text": "${ }^{52} \\mathrm{C}_4$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "nd21h",
              "text": "${ }^{52} \\mathrm{C}_2$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "duvKH",
              "text": "${ }^{48} \\mathrm{C}_4$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "PWCA7",
              "text": "${ }^{48} \\mathrm{C}_2$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "The given expression is $^{47}C_{4} + \\sum_{j=1}^{5} {}^{52-j}C_{3}$.<br><br>Expanding the summation, we get:<br><br>$^{47}C_{4} + ^{51}C_{3} + ^{50}C_{3} + ^{49}C_{3} + ^{48}C_{3} + ^{47}C_{3}$<br><br>Rearranging the terms:<br><br>$(^{47}C_{4} + ^{47}C_{3}) + ^{48}C_{3} + ^{49}C_{3} + ^{50}C_{3} + ^{51}C_{3}$<br><br>Using the identity $^{n}C_{r} + ^{n}C_{r-1} = ^{n+1}C_{r}$:<br><br>$^{47}C_{4} + ^{47}C_{3} = ^{48}C_{4}$<br><br>Substituting this back:<br><br>$^{48}C_{4} + ^{48}C_{3} + ^{49}C_{3} + ^{50}C_{3} + ^{51}C_{3}$<br><br>Applying the identity repeatedly:<br><br>$^{48}C_{4} + ^{48}C_{3} = ^{49}C_{4}$<br><br>$^{49}C_{4} + ^{49}C_{3} = ^{50}C_{4}$<br><br>$^{50}C_{4} + ^{50}C_{3} = ^{51}C_{4}$<br><br>$^{51}C_{4} + ^{51}C_{3} = ^{52}C_{4}$<br><br>Answer: ${ }^{52} \\mathrm{C}_4$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
