          "question": {
            "text": "If ${ }^{15} \\mathrm{C}_4+{ }^{15} \\mathrm{C}_5+{ }^{16} \\mathrm{C}_6+{ }^{17} \\mathrm{C}_7+{ }^{18} \\mathrm{C}_8={ }^{19} \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{r}}$, then the value of r is equal to",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "bUBC0",
              "text": "9 or 10",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "MXV8x",
              "text": "7 or 12",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "nN5fk",
              "text": "8 or 10",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "9rVPJ",
              "text": "8 or 11",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Using the identity $^{n}C_{r} + ^{n}C_{r-1} = ^{n+1}C_{r}$, we can simplify the given expression step by step.<br><br>$^{15}C_{4} + ^{15}C_{5} = ^{16}C_{5}$<br><br>Substituting this into the given equation:<br><br>$^{16}C_{5} + ^{16}C_{6} + ^{17}C_{7} + ^{18}C_{8} = ^{19}C_{r}$<br><br>$^{17}C_{6} + ^{17}C_{7} + ^{18}C_{8} = ^{19}C_{r}$<br><br>$^{18}C_{7} + ^{18}C_{8} = ^{19}C_{r}$<br><br>$^{19}C_{8} = ^{19}C_{r}$<br><br>We know that if $^{n}C_{x} = ^{n}C_{y}$, then either $x = y$ or $x + y = n$.<br><br>Therefore, $r = 8$ or $r = 19 - 8 = 11$.<br><br>Answer: 8 or 11",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
