          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "question": {
            "text": "The approximate value of $(0.007)^{\\frac{1}{3}}$ is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "y7dGF",
              "label": "A",
              "text": "$\\dfrac{21}{120}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "hbb3b",
              "label": "B",
              "text": "$\\dfrac{23}{120}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "SzlUa",
              "label": "C",
              "text": "$\\dfrac{29}{120}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "lJmmF",
              "label": "D",
              "text": "$\\dfrac{31}{120}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Let $f(x) = x^{\\dfrac{1}{3}}$<br><br>Let $x = 0.008$ and $\\Delta x = -0.001$<br><br>$f(x) = (0.008)^{\\dfrac{1}{3}} = 0.2 = \\dfrac{1}{5}$<br><br>$f'(x) = \\dfrac{1}{3} x^{-\\dfrac{2}{3}}$<br><br>$f'(0.008) = \\dfrac{1}{3(0.008)^{\\dfrac{2}{3}}} = \\dfrac{1}{3(0.04)} = \\dfrac{1}{0.12} = \\dfrac{100}{12} = \\dfrac{25}{3}$<br><br>Using the approximation $f(x + \\Delta x) \\approx f(x) + f'(x) \\Delta x$<br><br>$f(0.007) \\approx \\dfrac{1}{5} + \\left(\\dfrac{25}{3}\\right)(-0.001)$<br><br>$f(0.007) \\approx \\dfrac{1}{5} - \\dfrac{25}{3000}$<br><br>$f(0.007) \\approx \\dfrac{1}{5} - \\dfrac{1}{120}$<br><br>$f(0.007) \\approx \\dfrac{24 - 1}{120} = \\dfrac{23}{120}$<br><br>Answer: $\\dfrac{23}{120}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "previousYearPapers": [
