          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "If ${ }^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{C}_0+\\frac{1}{2}{ }^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{C}_1+\\frac{1}{3}{ }^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{C}_2+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots . . \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}}{ }^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{n}-1}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}+1}{ }^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\frac{1023}{10}$ then $\\mathrm{n}=$",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "GvuC3",
              "text": "7",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "z9vPH",
              "text": "8",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "n0a2U",
              "text": "9",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "SSSf3",
              "text": "10",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Consider the binomial expansion:<br><br>$(1+x)^n = ^{n}C_0 + ^{n}C_1 x + ^{n}C_2 x^2 + \\dots + ^{n}C_n x^n$<br><br>Integrating both sides with respect to $x$ from $0$ to $1$:<br><br>$\\int_{0}^{1} (1+x)^n dx = \\int_{0}^{1} (^{n}C_0 + ^{n}C_1 x + ^{n}C_2 x^2 + \\dots + ^{n}C_n x^n) dx$<br><br>$\\left[ \\dfrac{(1+x)^{n+1}}{n+1} \\right]_0^1 = \\left[ ^{n}C_0 x + ^{n}C_1 \\dfrac{x^2}{2} + ^{n}C_2 \\dfrac{x^3}{3} + \\dots + ^{n}C_n \\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1} \\right]_0^1$<br><br>$\\dfrac{2^{n+1}-1}{n+1} = ^{n}C_0 + \\dfrac{1}{2} ^{n}C_1 + \\dfrac{1}{3} ^{n}C_2 + \\dots + \\dfrac{1}{n+1} ^{n}C_n$<br><br>Given that the sum is equal to $\\dfrac{1023}{10}$, we have:<br><br>$\\dfrac{2^{n+1}-1}{n+1} = \\dfrac{1023}{10}$<br><br>Comparing the denominators, we can check $n+1 = 10 \\Rightarrow n = 9$.<br><br>Checking the numerator for $n = 9$:<br><br>$2^{9+1}-1 = 2^{10}-1 = 1024-1 = 1023$<br><br>This satisfies the equation perfectly.<br><br>Therefore, $n = 9$.<br><br>Answer: 9",
            "image": null
          },
